---
layout: base.njk
title: null
description: Sports writing and data visualisation — timelines, charts, and the wider context around the games.
---

<div class="wrap">

  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">{{ site.tagline }}</p>
    <h1>Sport doesn't happen in a vacuum.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Games are played against a backdrop of politics, money and policy. This site
      puts those threads on the same axis — so you can see what else was happening
      the year a record fell.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="grid grid-2">

    <a class="card card-link" href="{{ '/timeline/' | url }}">
      <p class="eyebrow">Interactive</p>
      <h3>The Timeline</h3>
      <p>
        {{ timeline.events | length }} events across {{ timeline.categories | length }} tracks,
        from {{ timeline.minYear | formatYear }} to {{ timeline.maxYear | formatYear }}. Filter by track, narrow the
        period, or overlay every track on a single axis.
      </p>
      <span class="card-cta">Open the timeline &rarr;</span>
    </a>

    <a class="card card-link" href="{{ '/data/' | url }}">
      <p class="eyebrow">Charts &amp; tools</p>
      <h3>Data &amp; Visual Tools</h3>
      <p>
        The datasets behind the site, how they are put together, and the tools used
        to check them before they are published.
      </p>
      <span class="card-cta">Browse the data &rarr;</span>
    </a>

  </div>

  <section class="card" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
    <h2 style="font-size:1.075rem">What's on the timeline</h2>
    <div class="stat-row" style="margin-top:0.9rem">
      {% for cat in timeline.categories %}
      <div class="stat">
        <div class="stat-label">{{ cat.name }}</div>
        <div class="stat-value">{{ cat.count }}</div>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

</div>
